# argon2kt's native code hands the computed hash back by writing ByteBufferTarget.byteBuffer, which
# it looks up by name over JNI. R8 cannot see that write. Without this rule it is free to rename the
# field, or — if no Java code is left writing it — to decide the field is always null and fold the
# reads away. Either way every passkey hash would fail in release builds while debug builds kept
# working. The class name itself is already kept, because it appears in a native method's signature.
-keep class com.lambdapioneer.argon2kt.ByteBufferTarget { *; }
